    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1173">

                <pb facs="1258" n="1162" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1162"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wos y Gil to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dominican Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New
                            York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-07-19"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 19, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to acknowledge receipt of your
                    communication of the 15th ultimo in reference to rules and suggestions to
                    neutral men-of-war entering or leaving blockaded ports.</p>
                <p>I have taken due note and will communicate same to my Government as soon as
                    possible.</p>
                <p>Please accept, sir, the renewed assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. y Gil</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
